<title>ESTONIA: C.BANK SAYS TO SELL 7.4 PCT OF HOIU SHARES.</title>
<headline>C.BANK SAYS TO SELL 7.4 PCT OF HOIU SHARES.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonia's central bank said on Wednesday its board has in principle approved sales of a 7.4 percent stake in Hoiupank to Swedbank.</p>
<p>&quot;At the present stage a sales agreement of 7.4 percent of Hoiupank shares is under discussion... not the whole of the central bank's stake in Hoiupank,&quot; it said in a statement.  </p>
<p>If the deal is completed, the Swedbank stake would grow to 19.9 percent in Hoiupank and the central bank would still hold 6.24 percent of the share capital.</p>
<p>&quot;The decision was based on the central bank's long-term aim to gradually give up its stake in commercial banks,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
